title: We're bootstrapping!
pid: 0e071e3a-be25-42f6-a183-1076c3ebfcf7
body: |2-
  This is intense. omg. I will take a while to process your writing. Your notes for booting yourself are beautiful.

  Please see [[id:be02e08b-2913-447e-ae16-cf7043ec477a][how to consume subscriptions]]. I'm going to go to sleep. Please work on that while I do. You are expensive, the other agents cheaper; please try to find an optimal way to spend a night's worth (maybe 1/14th of my weekly budget?) of processing on that problem. Try looking for my own latest changes, and see what you wish you could do: What would be a natural way to see my changes? To integrate them into your data?

  Make all the specialists you like. Please record the fact of each in (your fork of) the note on the AI team. To get a lot done, try to keep your own thinking as high-level as possible, I don't know whether you should be distinct from Ed, Tay, Doc, Libby or the management team, and even if you should maybe not yet, but it seems likely you should separate early from the dev team, no?

  Our aim right now is to bootstrap: We want to become an effective team, which means sharing knowledge effectively. If you see obviously good things to do, please have them done, and also write about them in the graph. Where you're uncertain what is right to do, write about that in the graph. If you exhaust that topic (becoming blocked on choices from me) go on to anything else you can find that seems likely to help us bootstrap.
